If you have any of the following, call 999 (do not drive yourself to A&E) [P82]:
- chest pain that feels tight or like squeezing on your chest;
- chest pain that's spreading to your arms, neck or jaw;
- severe difficulty breathing – you're gasping, choking or not able to get words out;
- lips or skin are pale, blue or grey (on brown or black skin this may be easier to see on the palms of the hands);
- someone has passed out and is not responding normally. [P82]

Call NHS 111 if you have any of the following [P84]:
- you're suddenly more short of breath than usual;
- you have chest pain and you feel sick or are being sick;
- you have chest pain and you feel like your heart is racing, going too slowly, skipping a beat or have a fluttering feeling in your chest. [P84]

